Architecture plan for Issues #130 and #131: direct dual cover-image upload

Project shape:
- Next.js App Router app using TypeScript, React, Tailwind CSS, Prisma/PostgreSQL, and S3-compatible object storage.
- Public reader routes live under app/(public); admin CMS routes, server actions, and post editor UI live under app/admin.
- Post persistence uses prisma/schema.prisma Post fields coverImageKey and squareCoverImageKey; upload/delete/signing helpers live in lib/storage/object-storage.ts.
- Admin post creation/update validation and upload orchestration live in app/admin/posts/actions.ts.

Relevant module/file organization:
- app/admin/posts/_components/post-editor-form.tsx owns the admin post form and should expose two normal file inputs: coverImage for 16:9 and squareCoverImage for 1:1.
- app/admin/posts/_components/cover-image-cropper.tsx currently owns client-side cropping, object URL previews, canvas export, hidden square input population, and submit replay; Issue #130 removes this component entirely.
- app/admin/posts/actions.ts already expects both coverImage and squareCoverImage File fields and enforces that a new/replacement cover upload includes both crops, so the server action can remain the integration point.
- tests/post-editor-upload-config.test.ts should become the primary unit/config guard for the direct-upload form shape.
- e2e/publish-public-view.spec.ts should upload both image fields directly instead of interacting with cropper controls.

Issue dependency analysis:
- Issue #130 is the implementation change: remove the cropper component and hidden square field, then add visible file inputs for both required cover image variants.
- Issue #131 depends on #130's final UI shape: tests and E2E flows should assert/use the two direct file inputs and remove cropper-specific expectations.
- No database, Prisma migration, storage API, or server action redesign is required because the existing data model and server actions already handle both image keys.

Key design decisions:
- Keep field names unchanged: coverImage and squareCoverImage, preserving compatibility with createPost/updatePost.
- Preserve multipart/form-data on the form and existing image accept list: image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp,image/gif.
- Remove client-side canvas/object URL/crop state complexity instead of leaving unused code paths.
- Keep publish validation behavior: published posts require both cover images and author avatar/name/intro; drafts may remain incomplete.
- Update tests after the UI change so they verify direct dual-image upload rather than cropper internals.
